    "abstract": "Tyrosinase (TYR) is the rate-limiting enzyme in melanin biosynthesis, and its overactivity is associated with hyperpigmentation disorders such as melasma and age spots. While synthetic inhibitors like hydroquinone (HQ) and kojic acid (KA) are conventional standards, their clinical utility is limited by high cytotoxicity, carcinogenicity, and skin irritation. This research project proposes a comprehensive in-silico comparative evaluation of four natural phytochemicals (arbutin, resveratrol, curcumin, and ellagic acid) against these synthetic standards. By utilizing AlphaFold3-predicted human tyrosinase (hTYR) and experimental mushroom tyrosinase (mTYR) structures, the study aims to identify safer, potent alternatives with superior transdermal permeability. The findings will establish a molecular and pharmacokinetic framework for the development of high-efficacy, \"green\" cosmeceuticals.",
