    "abstract": "Background: Pakistan is experiencing a serious epidemic of extensively drug-resistant (XDR) Salmonella Typhi, which is resistant to nearly all classical antibiotics. IV Meropenem and oral Azithromycin are used as clinical management. Purpose: The purpose of the objective is to assess the effects of a structured IV-to-Oral Switch (IVOS) on the hospital Length of Stay (LOS) and treatment expenses. Methodology: Retrospective, noninterventional, clinical audit on the Computerized Patient Record (CPR) system of the hospital. The data of the XDR typhoid patients (2021-2025) will be analyzed with the help of the validated clinical stability checklist. Outcome Measures: The main outcomes will consist of possible LOS reduction and direct cost-savings with the help of a Cost-Minimization Analysis (CMA). Conclusion:The proposed study aims to offer evidence-based data on the pharmacist-led antimicrobial stewardship to decrease the economic, clinical burden of XDR Typhoid in Pakistan.",
