    "abstract": "Obstructive sleep apnea (OSA) is a common but frequently underdiagnosed disorder, particularly among overweight individuals who are at increased risk of its associated complications, including cardiovascular disease, hypertension, and diabetes. Despite its clinical significance, awareness and screening uptake remain limited. This cross-sectional study aims to assess knowledge, risk perception, and screening readiness for Obstructive Sleep Apnea among overweight adults in Karachi. Data will be collected using a structured questionnaire to evaluate participants’ understanding of OSA, perceived personal susceptibility, and willingness to undergo screening. The STOP-BANG Questionnaire will be used to identify individuals at elevated risk and to compare objective risk status with perceived vulnerability and screening readiness. The study is expected to identify awareness gaps, possible barriers to screening, and differences between actual and perceived risk. Findings may contribute to the development of targeted educational strategies and community-based interventions to promote early detection and timely management of OSA among high-risk populations.",
