    "supervisor": "Dr Frahana Tasleem",
    "originalTitle": "Effects of Whole Wheat Extract on Blood Glucose Regulation in Albino Rats: A Preclinical Study",
    "abstract": "Rapid postprandial glucose spikes are associated with increased risk of insulin resistance, type 2 diabetes, and cardiovascular complications. Refined white flour is known to cause sharp glucose elevations due to its high glycaemic index and lack of dietary fiber, whereas whole wheat is hypothesized to attenuate this response. However, controlled experimental evidence in animal models is limited. The aim of this study is to compare the acute glycaemic response following oral administration of whole wheat flour vs. refined white flour in male Wistar rats.",
