    "originalTitle": "Evaluation of Waiting Time, Dispensing Errors, and the Role of Digital Technology in Hospital Pharmacy: An Online Survey-Based Study",
    "abstract": "Abstract \r\nThis study evaluates perceived waiting time and dispensing errors in hospital pharmacies using an online survey. Data were collected from patients, pharmacists, and pharmacy students through a structured questionnaire covering demographics, waiting time satisfaction, and experiences with dispensing errors.\r\nQuantitative data were analyzed using percentages and average scores, while qualitative responses were grouped into common themes. The study identifies key issues such as long waiting times and common dispensing errors, including wrong medication, dose, and instructions.\r\nFindings highlight the need for improvements in pharmacy workflow and patient safety. Recommended strategies include better queue management, increased staffing during peak hours, use of electronic prescription systems, staff training, and double-checking procedures.\r\nThis study provides practical insights to enhance efficiency and reduce errors in hospital pharmacy services.",
