    "originalTitle": "Knowledge and Use of Natural Supplements and Their Impact on Kidney Health Among the General Population and Their Clinical Implication",
    "abstract": "Abstract The use of natural supplements is increasingly common due to their perceived health benefits, yet their impact on kidney health remains underexplored. This study aims to assess the knowledge, patterns of use, and potential clinical implications of natural supplements among the general population, with a focus on renal health. A cross-sectional survey will be conducted using a structured questionnaire to collect information on participants’ awareness, types and frequency of supplement use, sources of information, and any kidney-related health concerns. Data will be analyzed using descriptive and inferential statistics to identify associations between supplement consumption and kidney function indicators. The findings are expected to highlight gaps in public knowledge, potential risks, and safe practices regarding supplement use. Clinically, the results will provide guidance for healthcare professionals to counsel patients, particularly those with pre-existing kidney conditions, on the safe and informed use of natural supplements, contributing to improved public health outcomes.\r\n\r\nObjectives:\r\n1. To assess the knowledge and awareness of natural supplements among the general population.\r\n2. To identify patterns of use, including types, frequency, and sources of natural supplements.\r\n3. To evaluate the potential impact of natural supplements on kidney health.\r\n4. To explore the clinical implications of supplement use, particularly for individuals with pre-existing renal conditions.\r\n\r\nMethodology:\r\nStudy Design: Cross-sectional survey.\r\nStudy Population: Adults (aged 18 and above) from diverse demographic and socio-economic backgrounds.\r\nSample Size: 300–500 participants.\r\nData Collection Tool: \r\nStructured questionnaire covering:\r\n• Awareness and knowledge of natural supplements\r\n• Types and frequency of supplements used\r\n• Reasons for use and sources of information\r\n• History of kidney-related health issues or conditions\r\nData Analysis:\r\n• Descriptive statistics (percentages, means, frequencies) to summarize data\r\n• Inferential statistics (chi-square test, correlation analysis) to identify associations between supplement use and kidney health indicators\r\nEthical Considerations: Participation will be voluntary, and informed consent will be obtained. Data confidentiality will be maintained.\r\n\r\nConclusion:\r\nThis study will provide insight into public knowledge and usage patterns of natural supplements and their potential effects on kidney health. The findings are expected to highlight knowledge gaps and risks associated with improper supplement use. Clinically, the study will help healthcare professionals counsel patients, especially those with kidney conditions, on safe and evidence-based use of natural supplements, ultimately contributing to improved renal health outcomes and public awareness.",
    "expertName": "",
