    "originalTitle": "Smart Pills Dispenser with Adherence Tracking by using digital tool to improve patient disease state",
    "abstract": "Abstract \r\nAim:\r\nTo develop a smart automated pill dispenser system that improves medication adherence through reminders and tracking.\r\n\r\nObjectives:\r\n\r\n● To design an automated pill dispensing mechanism\r\n● To integrate alert systems (alarm/mobile notification)\r\n● To track medication intake using sensors\r\n● To develop a system for recording and analyzing adherence data\r\n● To enhance patient compliance and reduce medication errors\r\n\r\nMethod\r\n\r\nThis project will use a combination of hardware and software components:\r\n\r\n● Hardware: Microcontroller (Arduino), motor system, pill compartments, sensors\r\n● Software: Mobile application or web dashboard for tracking\r\n● The dispenser will be programmed with medication schedules\r\n● Alerts will notify patients at dosing times\r\n● Sensors will detect whether medication is taken\r\n● Data will be stored and analyzed to monitor adherence\r\n\r\nResult\r\n\r\nThe expected result is a functional smart pill dispenser prototype capable of:\r\n\r\n● Delivering medication accurately and on time\r\n● Recording adherence data\r\n● Sending alerts and reminders\r\n● Providing reports for caregivers or healthcare professionals\r\n\r\nConclusion\r\n\r\nThe smart pill dispenser system can significantly improve medication adherence, especially in elderly and chronic patients. It offers a practical, technology-driven solution to reduce medication errors and enhance treatment outcomes. With further development, this system can be implemented in real healthcare settings.",
