    "originalTitle": "Development of a Pharmacy Consultant Services Web/App for Integrated Patient–Pharmacist–Clinician Connectivity",
    "abstract": "Abstract\r\nAim and Objectives: The aim of this project is to develop a centralized digital platform that connects patients, pharmacists, and clinicians to enhance accessibility, continuity, and quality of healthcare services. The objectives are to: (i) establish a structured communication channel for patient queries and professional consultation, (ii) enable pharmacist-led guidance for medication use and minor ailments, (iii) facilitate prescription sharing and validation between clinicians and pharmacists, and (iv) promote safe, rational, and accessible healthcare delivery through an integrated ecosystem. Method: A web/application-based platform was designed using a multi-user architecture consisting of dedicated interfaces for patients, pharmacists, and clinicians. Patients can submit health-related queries, upload prescriptions, and seek consultation through the platform. Pharmacists review patient concerns, provide evidence-based guidance for medication use, and identify cases requiring referral. Clinicians can access patient cases when needed and issue prescriptions directly within the system. The platform incorporates secure data handling, structured workflows, and user-friendly navigation to ensure efficient interaction between all stakeholders. The system was evaluated using simulated patient scenarios to assess workflow efficiency, response time, usability, and reliability of communication. Result: The developed prototype demonstrated effective coordination between patients, pharmacists, and clinicians within a single digital environment. The platform streamlined the consultation process, enabling timely pharmacist intervention and appropriate referral when necessary. It improved accessibility to professional pharmaceutical care, reduced delays in obtaining medication guidance, and minimized fragmentation in healthcare communication. User testing indicated that the system was intuitive and facilitated smoother interaction among all users, enhancing overall healthcare experience. Conclusion: The Pharmacy Consultant Services Web/App establishes a practical and scalable healthcare ecosystem that strengthens the role of pharmacists as accessible frontline healthcare providers. By integrating patients, pharmacists, and clinicians into a unified platform, the system improves communication, promotes rational drug use, and enhances continuity of care. This model has strong potential for real-world implementation and commercialization, particularly in settings where access to coordinated healthcare services remains limited",
