    "abstract": "This project proposes the development of an AI-based chatbot designed to assist individuals in interpreting their symptoms and making informed decisions about seeking healthcare. Many patients lack clarity about the seriousness of their symptoms and the type of healthcare professional they should consult, which often leads to unnecessary visits, increased costs, or delays in appropriate treatment. The proposed system aims to address this gap by allowing users to input symptoms and receive preliminary, evidence-based guidance on whether to seek emergency care, consult a specialist, or manage minor conditions through pharmacy advice. Unlike existing platforms, the chatbot’s key feature is its ability to recommend the most appropriate specialist based on symptom analysis rather than relying on patient self-selection. The system will be developed using reliable clinical and pharmaceutical data, with a phased plan focusing on research, prototype development, accuracy improvement, user accessibility, and eventual integration with healthcare platforms. Overall, the project aims to enhance early decision-making, improve healthcare access, and promote timely and appropriate medical consultation.",
