    "abstract": "Pain management remains a major concern in both clinical and community settings, particularly for patients who experience frequent musculoskeletal discomfort yet wish to avoid the systemic side effects associated with oral analgesics. This project focuses on the development and marketing strategy of a herbal pain relief patch formulated using natural bioactive ingredients known for their anti-inflammatory and analgesic properties. The aim is to introduce a noninvasive, easy-to-use, and sustained-release topical system designed to provide long-lasting relief from muscle, joint, and back pain. A comprehensive market assessment revealed a growing consumer shift toward herbal and self-care therapeutic options, alongside dissatisfaction with greasy topical formulations and gastrointestinal risks of oral NSAIDs. Guided by these insights, the product was positioned as a safe, convenient, and clinically relevant alternative. The marketing strategy combines healthcare professional engagement, digital promotion, brand differentiation, and a value-driven pricing model to establish strong market penetration. The project concludes that a herbal transdermal patch—supported by evidence-based claims, patientcentric design, and targeted promotional activities—holds significant potential in addressing unmet needs in pain management while creating a competitive footprint in the pharmaceutical marketplace.",
