    "abstract": "The “Aroma-Polymer Neuro Sensory Soothe Stones” represent a novel dual-sensory therapeutic concept integrating pharmaceutical controlled-release technology with neurosensory modulation. Unlike conventional aromatherapy products, these stones are fabricated using porous pharmaceutical-grade polymer or ceramic-clay composites impregnated with microencapsulated essential oils and herbal residues. Upon tactile stimulation (rubbing), frictional heat triggers sustained release of active volatile compounds, providing olfactory stimulation alongside touch-based distraction. This dual mechanism is grounded in the Gate Control Theory, offering potential benefits in stress relief, anxiety reduction, and cognitive relaxation. The product targets university students and professionals seeking portable, nonpharmacological soothing solutions.",
