    "originalTitle": "Design and Development of an AI-Enabled Urdu Mobile Application for Medicine Identification and Patient-Friendly Drug Information in Pakistan",
    "abstract": "In Pakistan, many patients struggle to follow their medical treatments safely because drug instructions and resources are almost exclusively written in English. This language barrier, combined with varying levels of health literacy, often leads to dangerous medication errors and poor adherence to treatment plans. To bridge this gap, this project proposes the development of an AI-enabled mobile application designed to provide medicine information in a way that is truly accessible to the local population. By using image recognition technology, users can simply scan a medicine's packaging to identify it and then receive clear, simplified instructions in Urdu.Beyond just text, the application features Urdu audio guidance to assist the elderly and those with limited literacy, ensuring that vital information regarding dosage, side effects, and safety precautions is understood by everyone. The platform is built to support a wide range of users, from someone needing a quick identification of a new pill to chronic patients and caregivers who require long-term management tools like medicine reminders and saved medication lists. Over a three-year roadmap, the project aims to evolve from a specialized database into a comprehensive digital health tool integrated with pharmacies and telehealth services. Ultimately, this initiative is about more than just technology; it is about empowering Pakistani patients with the knowledge they need to manage their health safely and effectively.",
