    "originalTitle": "Development and evaluation of the dual action of a zinc oxide-based dual action SPF formulation",
    "abstract": "The present project focuses on the formulation of a dual action cream containing zinc oxide and SPF for enhanced skin protection. Zinc oxide is a well-known physical sunblock that reflects and scatters harmful ultraviolet (UV) rays, while the SPF component provides additional photoprotective support against sun-induced skin damage.\r\n\r\nThe aim of this work was to prepare a stable, effective, and cosmetically acceptable cream formulation that can offer both broad-spectrum sun protection and skin barrier support in a single product.\r\n\r\nThe cream was designed using suitable emollients, emulsifying agents, and moisturizing ingredients to improve spread ability, consistency, and patient acceptability. Zinc oxide was incorporated as the main active ingredient due to its non-irritant and protective properties. The final formulation was evaluated for organoleptic characteristics, pH, homogeneity, spread ability, viscosity, and stability. cream showed good appearance, smooth texture, and acceptable physicochemical properties.\r\n\r\nThis dual action cream may serve as a promising topical formulation for daily skin protection, especially for individuals exposed to sunlight for prolonged periods. The study demonstrates the pharmaceutical potential of combining zinc oxide with SPF in a single cream to achieve enhanced protective efficacy and improved user convenience.",
