    "abstract": "The misuse of antibiotics for viral infections such as colds and flu is a major public health concern that contributes to antimicrobial resistance. Patient pressure on pharmacists to dispense antibiotics without a prescription is an important cause of inappropriate use. This proposed study aims to assess patient demand for non-prescription antibiotics in viral infections and evaluate their knowledge and attitudes regarding antibiotic use.\r\nA cross-sectional survey will be conducted among patients visiting community pharmacies using a structured questionnaire. Data will include frequency of antibiotic requests, reasons for demand, and awareness of antibiotic resistance.\r\nThe expected findings may help develop awareness programs, improve pharmacist counseling, and promote rational antibiotic use.",
