    "originalTitle": "Social Media Influence on Psychiatric Medication Use, Self-Medication, and Herbal/Allopathic Drug Practices in Anxiety, Depression, and Insomnia",
    "abstract": "Abstract\r\nSocial media platforms such as TikTok, Instagram, and YouTube have become major sources of health-related information, particularly in mental health awareness. Along with increasing awareness, these platforms also contribute to misinformation, leading to unsafe medication behaviors. This study investigates the influence of social media on psychiatric medication use among individuals experiencing symptoms of anxiety, depression, and insomnia. It further explores self-diagnosis behavior, where individuals label themselves as having anxiety or depression without clinical assessment, and subsequently initiate self-medication practices. These include the use of allopathic psychotropic drugs without prescription as well as herbal remedies as alternatives or supplements to prescribed therapy. The study aims to evaluate how digital exposure affects self-diagnosis, medication decisions, adherence patterns, and reliance on non-professional sources for treatment.",
