    "abstract": "Drug and Poison Information Centers (DPICs) play a crucial role in ensuring the safe and rational use of medications by providing accurate, evidence based information to healthcare professionals. However, in developing healthcare systems such as Pakistan, their utilization remains limited. This study aims to assess the level of awareness and utilization of DPICs among healthcare professionals in Karachi. The survey will be conducted among physicians, pharmacists, and nurses working in both public and private healthcare settings. Data will be collected using a structured, self administered questionnaire that will evaluate participants awareness, frequency of use, perceived benefits, and barriers to utilizing DPIC services.",
