    "abstract": "Muscle pain and stiffness are common health problems caused by stress, physical activity, injury, or prolonged sitting. Conventional pain relief methods often involve synthetic drugs, which may cause side effects with long-term use. Therefore, herbal-based therapeutic products are gaining popularity due to their safety, affordability, and natural origin. The present study aims to develop a Herbal Muscle Relaxant Pad using selected medicinal plant extracts known for their anti-inflammatory and analgesic properties. \r\n\r\nIn this study, herbal ingredients such as Peppermint(Mentha piperita), Ginger(Zingiber officinale), Turmeric(Curcuma longa) and Eucalyptus(Eucalyptus globulus) were selected due to their muscle-relaxant, anti-inflammatory, and soothing effects. The herbal extracts were prepared using a suitable solvent extraction method. A hydrogel-based pad was formulated by mixing the herbal extracts with a polymer base such as polyvinyl alcohol (PVA) or gelatin to provide flexibility and moisture retention. The mixture was poured into molds and allowed to dry to form soft, flexible pads.",
