    "originalTitle": "MyoNeuroChill Spray: Targeted Neuromuscular Cooling Therapy for Muscle Fatigue Relief",
    "abstract": "This study aims to develop and evaluate a herbal cooling spray for rapid and effective relief of muscle fatigue through targeted neuromuscular cooling. The formulation was prepared using a solvent-based technique in which menthol was dissolved in ethanol, followed by incorporation of peppermint and eucalyptus oils along with herbal extracts such as aloe vera, arnica, and ginger. Stabilizers including propylene glycol, glycerin, polysorbate 20, and vitamin E were added to enhance stability and skin compatibility. The final formulation was homogenized and filled into a spray container. Evaluation parameters include spray uniformity, cooling effect time, stability, and skin irritation. The formulation is expected to produce a rapid cooling effect within 1–3 minutes, ensure uniform spray distribution, and show no significant skin irritation, with improved muscle relaxation and reduction in fatigue symptoms. In conclusion, the developed herbal cooling spray is expected to be a safe, effective, and fast-acting solution for muscle fatigue relief, offering improved convenience and performance compared to conventional topical formulations.",
