    "abstract": "Background: Antimicrobial resistance (AMR) is a major global health problem.\r\nMisuse and overuse of antibiotics contribute to increasing resistance.\r\nLack of awareness about antimicrobial stewardship leads to unsafe practices (e.g., self-medication, incomplete courses).\r\nUse of herbal medicines is common, especially alongside conventional drugs.\r\nConcurrent use may lead to herbal-drug interactions.\r\nLimited public awareness about these interactions can affect treatment safety and effectiveness.\r\nThis study focuses on assessing awareness and practices related to these issues.",
