    "originalTitle": "Knowledge, Attitude, and Practice Regarding Herbal Medicine Use Among Pharmacy Students: A Survey-Based Study",
    "abstract": "Herbal medicines are extensively used for self-medication and form a fundamental component of pharmacognosy.\r\nDespite their widespread use, concerns persist regarding inadequate knowledge of their safety, efficacy, and potential herb–drug interactions, particularly among future healthcare professionals.\r\nThis study aims to assess the knowledge, attitude, and practice (KAP) of pharmacy students regarding herbal medicine use.\r\nA cross-sectional survey will be conducted using a structured questionnaire distributed among pharmacy students.\r\nThe questionnaire will evaluate patterns of use, awareness of therapeutic indications, knowledge of adverse effects and interactions, and overall perception of herbal medicines.\r\nData will be analyzed using descriptive statistics, including frequencies and percentages. The findings are expected to identify gaps in knowledge and variations in usage patterns, thereby emphasizing the need for improved educational strategies in pharmacognosy.\r\nThis study will contribute to promoting rational and evidence-based use of herbal medicines in future pharmacy practice.",
