    "abstract": "The COVID-19 pandemic increased awareness about immunity, leading to greater use of herbal immunity boosters among the general population. This study aimed to assess knowledge and usage patterns of commonly used herbal products such as ginger, turmeric, and honey. A cross-sectional survey was conducted using a structured questionnaire. The findings showed that many participants were aware of and regularly used herbal remedies, mainly influenced by social media and traditional practices. However, gaps in accurate knowledge and proper usage were observed. In conclusion, although the use of herbal immunity boosters has increased after COVID-19, there is a need for proper awareness to ensure safe and effective use.",
