    "abstract": "This pharmacognosy project focuses on the preparation and evaluation of a herbal blood-purifying drink from Fagonia cretica (Dhamasa Booti), a plant traditionally used in herbal medicine. The drink was prepared by boiling dried plant material in water, followed by filtration and optional flavoring.\r\nThe formulation was evaluated for its physical properties, pH, and phytochemical constituents such as flavonoids, tannins, and saponins. These compounds are known for their antioxidant and anti-inflammatory activities, which support its traditional use as a blood purifier.\r\nThe results suggest a link between the traditional claims and scientific properties of the plant. However, further studies are needed to confirm its safety and effectiveness.",
