    "originalTitle": "Formulation and Evaluation of a Polyherbal Antioxidant Sunscreen Gel for Natural Photoprotection",
    "abstract": "This project focuses on the formulation and evaluation of a polyherbal sunscreen gel using easily available herbal ingredients to develop a cost effective and natural photoprotective product. The gel was prepared using Aloe vera gel for skin hydration and soothing effect, Daucus carota (carrot) extract as a natural UV-protective agent, and Camellia sinensis (green tea) extract for antioxidant activity. Carbopol 940 was used as the gel base to ensure proper consistency, smooth application, and non-greasy texture. The formulation was evaluated for pH, spreadability, viscosity, and physical stability over a period of time. The study aims to provide a safe and cosmetically acceptable herbal sunscreen gel, suitable for daily use, while integrating multiple herbal extracts for enhanced photoprotection. The results showed that the gel was stable, easy to apply, and visually appealing, highlighting the practical application of traditional herbal knowledge in modern topical formulations. This project demonstrates an innovative approach to herbal photoprotection that can be implemented in a standard laboratory setting.",
