    "originalTitle": "Formulation and Evaluation of a Herbal-Probiotic Powder for Management of Irritable Bowel Syndrome (IBS)",
    "abstract": "Abstract:\r\nThis project aims to develop a herbal-probiotic powder combining ginger, fennel, peppermint, and Lactobacillus probiotics to support gut health and relieve IBS symptoms. The formulation demonstrates the synergistic effect of medicinal herbs and probiotics, providing a natural, plant-based approach to digestive well-being.\r\nBackground:\r\nIrritable Bowel Syndrome (IBS) is a common gastrointestinal disorder caused by gut microbiota imbalance and digestive disturbances. Traditional herbs such as ginger, fennel, and peppermint improve digestion, while probiotics restore healthy gut flora. Combining these offers a plant-based, natural solution for IBS management.\r\nObjectives:\r\nDevelop a herbal-probiotic powder targeting IBS.\r\nHighlight pharmacognostic properties of selected herbs.\r\nDemonstrate the synergistic effect of probiotics and herbs in digestive support.\r\nMethodology:\r\nDry and grind ginger, fennel, and peppermint into fine powder.\r\nMix the herbal powders uniformly.\r\nCarefully add Lactobacillus probiotics, avoiding moisture and heat.\r\nOptionally add inulin (prebiotic) or sugar/flavor.\r\nPackage in airtight sachets or capsules labeled Herbal-Probiotic Powder for IBS.\r\nExpected Outcomes:\r\nStable, dry, and palatable herbal-probiotic powder.\r\nHerbs aid digestion; probiotics help restore gut microbiota.\r\nDemonstrates a natural, plant-based approach for IBS symptom relief.\r\nConclusion:\r\nThis project combines medicinal herbs and probiotics to create a functional, natural formulation for IBS management. It emphasizes pharmacognosy principles, highlighting the therapeutic potential of plants while addressing gut microbiome health.",
