    "courseCode": "PHM-409",
    "courseTitle": "Quality Management",
    "supervisor": "Zoya Amin",
    "originalTitle": "What are the most frequently purchased classes of over-the-counter (OTC) drugs in \r\ncommunity pharmacies located in commercial vs. residential areas of Karachi?",
    "abstract": "OVER-THE-COUNTER (OTC) DRUGS ARE MEDICATIONS THAT CAN BE PURCHASED OVER-THE-COUNTER (OTC) DRUGS ARE MEDICATIONS THAT CAN BE PURCHASED WITHOUT A PRESCRIPTION AND ARE WIDELY USED FOR THE MANAGEMENT OF WITHOUT A PRESCRIPTION AND ARE WIDELY USED FOR THE MANAGEMENT OF MINOR AILMENTS SUCH AS PAIN, FEVER, ALLERGIES, AND GASTROINTESTINAL MINOR AILMENTS SUCH AS PAIN, FEVER, ALLERGIES, AND GASTROINTESTINAL DISTURBANCES. IN DEVELOPING COUNTRIES LIKE PAKISTAN, OTC DRUGS PLAY A DISTURBANCES. IN DEVELOPING COUNTRIES LIKE PAKISTAN, OTC DRUGS PLAY A SIGNIFICANT ROLE IN SELF-MEDICATION PRACTICES DUE TO EASY ACCESSIBILITY AND SIGNIFICANT ROLE IN SELF-MEDICATION PRACTICES DUE TO EASY ACCESSIBILITY AND LIMITED HEALTHCARE RESOURCES.",
    "expertName": "",
