    "originalTitle": "Development and in vitro Evaluation of a Temperature-responsive Multifunctional Hydrogel Patch Using Modified Commercial Cooling Patch for Sleep Enhancement.",
    "abstract": "Insomnia is a prevalent disorder often managed with oral sedatives that carry risks of dependency and systemic side effects. This project proposes a non-invasive, innovative solution: a temperature-responsive multifunctional hydrogel patch. By modifying a commercial cooling patch, the original gel layer is replaced with a custom-formulated hydrogel matrix composed of Carbopol 940 and Polyvinyl Alcohol (PVA), loaded with lavender and chamomile essential oils. The patch is designed to retain its inherent cooling effect while providing controlled, temperature-triggered aromatherapy to promote relaxation. The formulation utilizes ethanol for oil dispersion and triethanolamine for stabilization. Evaluation will focus on physical homogeneity, pH compatibility, and the duration of aroma release. This study demonstrates a feasible, cost-effective method to achieve controlled-release drug delivery and skin hydration, offering a safe alternative for sleep enhancement.",
