    "originalTitle": "Formulation and Evaluation of Urea-Based Moisturizing Cream (10%) for Dry skin",
    "abstract": "Skin dryness (xerosis) is a common condition marked by rough, scaly, and itchy skin, affecting people worldwide, especially the elderly and patients with diabetes or eczema. In Pakistan, its prevalence is increased due to environmental factors, pollution, and limited access to proper skincare. Current treatments include emollients, humectants, and topical corticosteroids, along with moisturizers containing glycerin, lactic acid, and urea. Urea is particularly effective due to its keratolytic and hydrating properties, which enhance moisture retention and skin barrier function. \r\nThis study focuses on the formulation and evaluation of a 10% urea-based moisturizing cream as an affordable treatment for dry skin. The formulation will be assessed through tests such as pH, viscosity, spreadability, stability, microbial evaluation, and skin hydration. The expected outcome is a stable, safe, and cost-effective cream that improves skin hydration and is easily accessible in Pakistan.",
