    "originalTitle": "Design and Evaluation of medicated Lollipop containing Amylmetacresol for the treatment of Sore thoart",
    "abstract": "Sore throat (pharyngitis) is a highly prevalent upper respiratory condition that significantly affects patient comfort and quality of life, often requiring localized antimicrobial therapy for effective symptomatic relief. Amylmetacresol (AMC), a well-established antiseptic agent, is widely used for managing oropharyngeal infections; however, conventional dosage forms such as lozenges may provide limited residence time and suboptimal sustained drug release. The present study aims to design, formulate, and evaluate a medicated lollipop containing AMC as a novel, patient-friendly drug delivery system intended to enhance buccal retention, improve palatability, and ensure controlled drug release. The formulation will be prepared using a heated syrup base composed of sucrose and liquid glucose, with incorporation of AMC and suitable flavoring and stabilizing agents. Comprehensive evaluation will include weight variation, hardness, friability, drug content uniformity, moisture content analysis, and in vitro dissolution studies to determine release kinetics. Expected outcomes include a stable lollipop achieving >80% AMC release within 15 minutes, potent antibacterial activity (MIC <4 µg/mL), and superior symptom relief compared to conventional lozenges.",
