    "abstract": "Insulin requires strict refrigeration (2–8 °C), a logistical barrier in many parts of the world. This project proposes the synthesis of a Polymer-Lipid Hybrid Nanoparticle (PLHN) system. By encapsulating insulin within a solid lipid core protected by a chitosan-modified shell, we aim to prevent the thermal denaturation and fibrillation of the peptide.\r\n3. Introduction \r\n• The Problem: High ambient temperatures lead to insulin \"unfolding\" (fibrillation), reducing its efficacy and potentially causing immune reactions.\r\n• The Goal: To design a nano-carrier that shields insulin from heat-induced mechanical and chemical stress.\r\n4. Objectives:\r\n• Synthesize insulin-loaded nanoparticles using biocompatible polymers (e.g., Acetylated Inulin or Chitosan) and lipids (e.g., Stearic acid).\r\n• Evaluate the Encapsulation Efficiency (EE) and particle size distribution.\r\n• Measure insulin stability at 37°C and 45°C over a 90-day period.\r\n• Conduct in vivo studies to compare the glycemic control of the nanoformulation vs. standard insulin.",
