    "originalTitle": "Formulation and Evaluation of Medicated Chocolate Infused with Cinnamon (Cinnamomum zeylanicum) Extract as a Novel Herbal Antidiabetic Dosage Form",
    "abstract": "The increasing prevalence of diabetes has driven the need for effective, natural, and patient-friendly therapeutic options. This study presents the formulation and evaluation of a medicated chocolate infused with Cinnamon (Cinnamomum zeylanicum) extract as a novel herbal antidiabetic dosage form. Cinnamon is widely recognized for its insulin-sensitizing and glucose-lowering properties, making it a suitable candidate for such formulations. The extract was incorporated into a chocolate base to enhance palatability and improve patient compliance, especially in pediatric and geriatric populations. The prepared formulations were evaluated for physicochemical parameters including appearance, texture, melting point, weight variation, and drug content. In vitro release studies were conducted to analyze the release behavior of active constituents, along with stability testing under various conditions. The results indicated satisfactory quality, stability, and promising antidiabetic potential, suggesting that medicated chocolate could serve as an innovative alternative to conventional dosage forms.",
