    "originalTitle": "Polyherbal Anti-Pollution Antioxidant Tablet",
    "abstract": "Air pollution is a major environmental health concern associated with increased oxidative stress, inflammation, and respiratory disorders. The present study focuses on the development of a polyherbal antioxidant tablet designed to mitigate the harmful effects of pollution on both pulmonary and systemic health. The formulation combines standardized extracts of Moringa oleifera, Camellia sinensis (green tea), Curcuma longa, Ocimum sanctum (Tulsi), and Piper nigrum, selected for their potent antioxidant, anti-inflammatory, and adaptogenic properties. \r\nThe tablet is formulated using suitable excipients to ensure stability, palatability, and patient compliance, with film coating applied to mask bitterness and enhance acceptability. Standardization of key bioactive markers such as curcumin and epigallocatechin gallate (EGCG) is incorporated to ensure batch-to-batch consistency and therapeutic efficacy. The formulation is evaluated for physicochemical parameters, antioxidant activity (e.g., DPPH assay), and in vitro release profile. \r\nThis study aims to provide a novel pharmacognosy-based approach for combating pollution-induced oxidative damage, addressing a significant gap in preventive healthcare. The developed polyherbal tablet has the potential to serve as a supportive therapeutic option for individuals exposed to high levels of environmental pollutants.",
