    "supervisor": "Shahnila Jamil",
    "originalTitle": "Formulation, Phytochemical Standardization, and In-Vitro Evaluation of a Synergistic Moringa-Fenugreek \"Gluco-Shield\" Tea for Glycemic Management.",
    "abstract": "The global rise in Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus and pre-diabetes necessitates effective strategies for controlling postprandial hyperglycemia to prevent long-term complications. This study aims to formulate and evaluate a functional herbal tea, “Gluco-Shield,” based on the synergistic effects of Moringa oleifera and Trigonella foenum-graecum.\r\nFenugreek seeds are a rich source of galactomannan, a soluble fiber that forms a viscous gel in the gastrointestinal tract, thereby reducing the rate of glucose absorption. Moringa leaves contain bioactive compounds such as quercetin and chlorogenic acid, which contribute to glycemic regulation through antioxidant activity and modulation of carbohydrate-metabolizing enzymes.\r\nShade-dried Moringa leaves and roasted Fenugreek seeds were processed and combined in three different ratios (50:50, 70:30, and 30:70). The formulations were extracted in hot water at 90°C for 10 minutes to simulate typical tea preparation conditions. Phytochemical standardization was carried out using qualitative tests, including mucilage test for polysaccharides, froth test for saponins, and ferric chloride test for phenolic compounds.\r\nThe study emphasizes the concept of synergistic phytochemical interaction in contrast to conventional single-herb formulations. The optimized formulation is expected to demonstrate enhanced antioxidant potential, significant mucilage formation, and acceptable organoleptic properties, indicating its potential as a supportive dietary intervention for glycemic management.",
