    "abstract": "This study explores the development of a sublingual bioadhesive glucose film designed as a rapid first-aid intervention for acute hypoglycemia. By utilizing a solvent-casting technique with bioadhesive polymers, the film is engineered to adhere securely to the sublingual mucosa, ensuring immediate glucose absorption directly into the systemic circulation while bypassing the gastrointestinal tract. This delivery method offers a critical advantage over traditional oral treatments by providing a faster glycemic response and reducing choking risks for patients with impaired consciousness. Experimental results indicate that the optimized formulation achieves rapid disintegration and sustained adhesion, demonstrating its potential as a portable, efficient, and user-friendly solution for emergency blood sugar management.",
