    "originalTitle": "Synergistic Herbal Approach to Alopecia: Development of a Topical Emulsion Gel.",
    "abstract": "A polyherbal emulsion gel was developed using an oil-in-water Carbopol matrix with extracts from 11 medicinal plants, including Azadirachta indica, Aloe barbadensis, Zingiber officinale, and Hibiscus rosa-sinensis, as a safer alternative to synthetic alopecia treatments. The gel exhibited suitable consistency, scalp-friendly pH, good stability, and no phase separation. User-reported outcomes from alopecia subjects, validated via Cronbach’s alpha and chi-square analysis, showed significant associations confirming user satisfaction. In this study protocol, a testosterone-induced alopecia mouse model will be used over a 21-day period to evaluate the anti-alopecia efficacy of a polyherbal formulation, with daily topical application of the respective treatments. To conclude this polyherbal formulation is a safe, effective, and user-friendly topical formulation with promising potential for alopecia management through synergistic herbal delivery.",
